til end of turn.","power":"2","produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2019-01-25","toughness":"1","type_line":"Creature — Insect"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"If a token is exiled this way, it will cease to exist and won't return to the battlefield.","oracle_id":"0f68ae67-1671-4281-8b6b-3e52fdd4915f","published_at":"2024-07-26","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Once the exiled permanent returns, it's considered a new object with no relation to the object that it was. Auras attached to the exiled permanent will be put into their owners' graveyards. Equipment attached to the exiled permanent will become unattached and remain on the battlefield. Any counters on the exiled permanent will cease to exist.","oracle_id":"0f68ae67-1671-4281-8b6b-3e52fdd4915f","published_at":"2024-07-26","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Because tokens aren't cards, they never count for undergrowth abilities.","oracle_id":"332b6ed7-90de-46c0-85ad-1ad708b2c1e1","published_at":"2018-10-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Creature cards with other types, such as artifact creature cards, count for undergrowth abilities.","oracle_id":"332b6ed7-90de-46c0-85ad-1ad708b2c1e1","published_at":"2018-10-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you choose a target and the target creature is an illegal target when Kraul Harpooner's ability tries to resolve, the ability doesn't resolve and Kraul Harpooner doesn't get +X/+0. If the target creature is legal but Kraul Harpooner is no longer on the battlefield, the target creature won't deal or be dealt damage.","oracle_id":"332b6ed7-90de-46c0-85ad-1ad708b2c1e1","published_at":"2018-10-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you don't choose a target creature, Kraul Harpooner simply gets +X/+0 until end of turn.","oracle_id":"332b6ed7-90de-46c0-85ad-1ad708b2c1e1","published_at":"2018-10-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The value of X is determined only as the undergrowth ability resolves. If the number of creature cards in your graveyard changes later in the turn, Kraul Harpooner is unaffected.","oracle_id":"332b6ed7-90de-46c0-85ad-1ad708b2c1e1","published_at":"2018-10-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You choose the target of the triggered ability (or that it has no target) as it goes on the stack, but you choose whether the creatures fight as that ability resolves.","oracle_id":"332b6ed7-90de-46c0-85ad-1ad708b2c1e1","published_at":"2018-10-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Spire Mangler can be the target of its own ability.","oracle_id":"6416dae0-0d40-4d88-b30b-e1a0c8380e78","published_at":"2019-01-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"To work as an evasion ability, an attacking creature must already have flying when the declare blockers step begins. Once a creature has become blocked, giving it flying won’t change that.","oracle_id":"f7518456-45ed-41d4-bd3c-5aacea28eb35","published_at":"2009-10-01","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
